# skeepto-engine — C++ naming and types

Code lives in `namespace SkRoot`. Files are `Sk*.hpp` / `Sk*.cpp`. C++ types are `t…`, not `Sk…`. Comments in American English.

## Prefixes

| Prefix | Role | Examples |
|--------|------|----------|
| `t` | Types, classes, enums, typedefs | `tInt`, `tString`, `tClassInt`, `tVariant` |
| `s` | **Stack** — all function parameters (in and out) | `sValue`, `sFormatString`, `sOut` |
| `w` | **Work** — local variables | `wStream`, `wResult`, `wIndex` |
| `m_` | Class **members** | `m_Value`, `m_Type` |
| `c` / `k` | Constants | `cSlash`, `kEncodeTable` |

Never use an `o` prefix. An output parameter is still stack: `tString& sOut`, not `oOut`.

Method **names** are PascalCase (`Encode`, `IsNumber`). Do **not** prefix them with `s`. A parameter named after its type drops the `t`: `const tVariant& sVariant`.

```cpp
tString Foo(const tString& sName, tSize sSize, tString& sOut) {
    tString wResult;
    tSize wIndex = 0;
    // ...
    sOut = wResult;
    return wResult;
}
```

## Types (`Libraries/SkRoot/include/SkTypes.hpp`)

Do **not** use raw `int`, `bool`, `double`, `std::string` in engine code. Use:

`tInt` `tUInt` `tSize` `tShort` `tUShort` `tByte` `tUByte` `tLong` `tLongLong` `tBool` `tFloat` `tDouble` `tChar` `tString` `tDate` `tIndex` `tColor` `tAllocatorRef`

Containers: `tVectorString`, `tVectorInt`, `tVectorSize`, `tStackInt`, `tStringStream`. Macros: `SkMin` `SkMax` `SkAlign` `SkInline`.

Enums are `enum class` with a `t` name; enumerators often use `t_…` (`tVariantType::t_int`, `tTypeError::t_div0`).

## Boxing (`Libraries/SkRoot/include/SkTypesClass.hpp`)

`tClassInt` `tClassFloat` `tClassDouble` `tClassString` `tClassDate` `tClassError` inherit `tClass` (C# boxing). Payload is `m_Value`.

- **Box:** `tClassInt wInt(42);` `tClassString wText("hello");`
- **Unbox:** `tInt wRaw = wInt();` — `operator()` returns the primitive
- `Str()` → `tString`; `FormatString(tFormatString*)` formats via `tClassFormatString<T>`
- Arithmetic / compare operators stay on the boxed type
- `tClassString`: `Left` `Trim` `Split` `Replace` `IsNumber` `ToInt` `ToDouble` …
- `tClassDate`: Excel serial days; can construct from `tVariant`
- `tClassError`: spreadsheet errors (`tTypeError`)

Cell values use `tVariant` (16-byte tagged union: `m_Type`, `m_Extra`, `m_Union`). Setters take `sValue`.
